{'review': '{\n  "review": {\n    "overall_status": "NEEDS_FIXES",\n    "quality_score": 3.2,\n    "summary": {\n      "critical": 1,\n      "high": 5,\n      "medium": 2,\n      "low": 0,\n      "passed_checks": [\n        "UUID primary keys for global uniqueness",\n        "TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE for consistent time handling",\n        "Default NOW() for timestamps",\n        "Unique indexes on natural keys (GitHub IDs)",\n        "Foreign keys with CASCADE for referential integrity"\n      ]\n    },\n    "findings": [\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-001",\n        "severity": "critical",\n        "category": "security",\n        "title": "API keys stored in plain text",\n        "file": "migrations/001_create_users.sql",\n        "line_range": [112, 112],\n        "description": "The \'key\' column in the \'api_keys\' table stores API keys in plain text (VARCHAR(255)). If the database is compromised, all API keys are exposed, allowing attackers to impersonate users and access their GitHub accounts or other services.",\n        "impact": "Complete breach of user API keys leading to unauthorized access to connected services (e.g., GitHub), potential data theft, and account takeover. Violates security best practices for secret storage.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Application must hash API keys before storage (e.g., using bcrypt or Argon2). Store only the hash in this table. Consider adding a comment to document this requirement.",\n        "code_before": "    \\"key\\" VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,",\n        "code_after": "    \\"key\\" VARCHAR(255) NOT NULL,  -- APPLICATION MUST STORE A HASH OF THE API KEY (E.G., BCRYPT), NOT THE PLAIN KEY",\n        "references": [\n          "CWE-798: Use of Hard-coded Credentials",\n          "OWASP A02:2021 – Cryptographic Failures",\n          "NIST SP 800-63B: Memorized Secret Verifiers"\n        ]\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-002",\n        "severity": "high",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "Missing index on foreign key column repositories.user_id",\n        "file": "migrations/001_create_users.sql",\n        "line_range": [34, 34],\n        "description": "The foreign key column \'user_id\' in the \'repositories\' table lacks an index. This forces full table scans during JOINs with the \'users\' table and during cascading DELETE operations when a user is removed.",\n        "impact": "As the repositories table grows, queries fetching a user\'s repositories (JOIN) and user deletions (triggering CASCADE deletes) will degrade to O(n) performance, causing slow response times and potential timeouts.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Add a non-unique index on the \'user_id\' column to optimize JOINs and cascading operations.",\n        "code_before": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"repositories_github_repo_id_key\\" ON \\"repositories\\"(\\"github_repo_id\\");",\n        "code_after": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"repositories_github_repo_id_key\\" ON \\"repositories\\"(\\"github_repo_id\\");\\nCREATE INDEX \\"repositories_user_id_idx\\" ON \\"repositories\\"(\\"user_id\\");",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-003",\n        "severity": "high",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "Missing index on foreign key column commits.repo_id",\n        "file": "migrations/001_create_users.sql",\n        "line_range": [58, 58],\n        "description": "The foreign key column \'repo_id\' in the \'commits\' table lacks an index. This impacts performance when fetching commits for a repository (JOIN) and when deleting a repository (triggering CASCADE deletes on commits).",\n        "impact": "Slow performance for repository-specific commit history queries and repository deletion operations. As commit volume increases, these operations become increasingly inefficient.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Add an index on the \'repo_id\' column to support efficient lookups and cascading deletes.",\n        "code_before": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"commits_sha_key\\" ON \\"commits\\"(\\"sha\\");",\n        "code_after": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"commits_sha_key\\" ON \\"commits\\"(\\"sha\\");\\nCREATE INDEX \\"commits_repo_id_idx\\" ON \\"commits\\"(\\"repo_id\\");",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-004",\n        "severity": "high",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "Missing index on foreign key column pull_requests.repo_id",\n        "file": "migrations/001_create_users.sql",\n        "line_range": [81, 81],\n        "description": "The foreign key column \'repo_id\' in the \'pull_requests\' table lacks an index. This affects performance when retrieving pull requests for a repository and when deleting a repository (CASCADE deletes on pull requests).",\n        "impact": "Degraded performance for repository-based pull request listings and repository cleanup operations. Particularly problematic for active repositories with many pull requests.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Add an index on the \'repo_id\' column to optimize repository-scoped queries and cascading deletions.",\n        "code_before": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"pull_requests_github_pr_id_key\\" ON \\"pull_requests\\"(\\"github_pr_id\\");",\n        "code_after": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"pull_requests_github_pr_id_key\\" ON \\"pull_requests\\"(\\"github_pr_id\\");\\nCREATE INDEX \\"pull_requests_repo_id_idx\\" ON \\"pull_requests\\"(\\"repo_id\\");",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-005",\n        "severity": "high",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "Missing index on foreign key column issues.repo_id",\n        "file": "migrations/001_create_users.sql",\n        "line_range": [103, 103],\n        "description": "The foreign key column \'repo_id\' in the \'issues\' table lacks an index. This hinders performance when querying issues by repository and when deleting a repository (CASCADE deletes on issues).",\n        "impact": "Inefficient repository-specific issue tracking and repository deletion processes. Performance degrades linearly with the number of issues per repository.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Create an index on the \'repo_id\' column to accelerate repository-based issue queries and cascading deletes.",\n        "code_before": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"issues_github_issue_id_key\\" ON \\"issues\\"(\\"github_issue_id\\");",\n        "code_after": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"issues_github_issue_id_key\\" ON \\"issues\\"(\\"github_issue_id\\");\\nCREATE INDEX \\"issues_repo_id_idx\\" ON \\"issues\\"(\\"repo_id\\");",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-006",\n        "severity": "high",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "Missing index on foreign key column api_keys.user_id",\n        "file": "migrations/001_create_users.sql",\n        "line_range": [120, 120],\n        "description": "The foreign key column \'user_id\' in the \'api_keys\' table has no index. This slows down lookups of API keys by user (e.g., during authentication) and cascading deletions when a user is removed.",\n        "impact": "Authentication checks involving API key validation become slower as the user base grows. User deletion operations (which should clean up associated API keys) suffer from poor performance.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Add an index on the \'user_id\' column to optimize user-based API key lookups and cascading delete operations.",\n        "code_before": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"api_keys_key_key\\" ON \\"api_keys\\"(\\"key\\");",\n        "code_after": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"api_keys_key_key\\" ON \\"api_keys\\"(\\"key\\");\\nCREATE INDEX \\"api_keys_user_id_idx\\" ON \\"api_keys\\"(\\"user_id\\");",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-007",\n        "severity": "medium",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "Missing composite index on pull_requests(repo_id, number)",\n        "file": "migrations/001_create_users.sql",\n        "line_range": [81, 81],\n        "description": "While the \'github_pr_id\' is unique, common queries filter by \'repo_id\' and \'number\' (the pull request number within a repository). Without a composite index, these queries require scanning the entire table or using less efficient single-column indexes.",\n        "impact": "Slower performance for API endpoints that retrieve a specific pull request by repository and number (e.g., GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/pulls/{number}). This is a frequent operation in GitHub client applications.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Add a composite index on (repo_id, number) to optimize the most common query pattern for pull requests.",\n        "code_before": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"pull_requests_github_pr_id_key\\" ON \\"pull_requests\\"(\\"github_pr_id\\");",\n        "code_after": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"pull_requests_github_pr_id_key\\" ON \\"pull_requests\\"(\\"github_pr_id\\");\\nCREATE INDEX \\"pull_requests_repo_id_number_idx\\" ON \\"pull_requests\\"(\\"repo_id\\", \\"number\\");",\n        "references": []\n      },\n      {\n        "finding_id": "F-008",\n        "severity": "medium",\n        "category": "performance",\n        "title": "Missing composite index on issues(repo_id, number)",\n        "file": "migrations/001_create_users.sql",\n        "line_range": [103, 103],\n        "description": "Similar to pull requests, issues are frequently queried by repository and issue number. The absence of a composite index on (repo_id, number) forces inefficient access patterns for this common use case.",\n        "impact": "Reduced performance for retrieving specific issues by repository and number (e.g., GET /repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues/{number}), a core operation in issue tracking systems.",\n        "suggested_fix": "Create a composite index on (repo_id, number) to speed up repository-scoped issue lookups by number.",\n        "code_before": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"issues_github_issue_id_key\\" ON \\"issues\\"(\\"github_issue_id\\");",\n        "code_after": "CREATE UNIQUE INDEX \\"issues_github_issue_id_key\\" ON \\"issues\\"(\\"github_issue_id\\");\\nCREATE INDEX \\"issues_repo_id_number_idx\\" ON \\"issues\\"(\\"repo_id\\", \\"number\\");",\n        "references": []\n      }\n    ],\n    "positive_observations": [\n      "UUID primary keys ensure global uniqueness and avoid sequence bottlenecks in distributed systems",\n      "Consistent use of TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE prevents timezone-related data inconsistencies",\n      "Default VALUES NOW() for created_at/updated_at timestamps reduces application-side errors",\n      "Unique indexes on GitHub IDs (username, repo_id, pr_id, issue_id) prevent duplicate entries from API syncs",\n      "Foreign key constraints with ON DELETE CASCADE maintain referential integrity and automate cleanup"\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```'}